# Mercenta Commerce — environment template
# Copy to .env.local and fill in. NEVER commit real keys.

# Supabase (browser-safe anon key only; service-role key stays server-side)
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# §PHASE B (2026-10-13) — REMOVED: VITE_OPENROUTER_API_KEY, VITE_HUNTER_API_KEY,
# VITE_INSTANTLY_API_KEY.
#
# WHY THEY WERE REMOVED. Vite copies every VITE_* value into the JavaScript the
# browser downloads. A provider key set that way would therefore be readable by
# anyone who opened the site — no login needed — and would stay readable inside
# the built files after the variable was unset, because the key is baked into
# the build output.
#
# WHERE PROVIDER KEYS GO NOW. Into Supabase Vault, server-side, through the
# Integrations connect wizard. The browser receives only a reference name
# (`vault:<name>`); it can ask `integration-secrets-status` whether a key EXISTS
# and gets a yes/no, never a value. See `supabase/functions/_shared/vault.ts`.

# NOTE: per §14, provider credentials for Amazon SP-API / Stripe / DocuSign /
# Postmark etc. are managed through the Integrations wizard and stored encrypted
# server-side — they do NOT belong in this file.
